From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fexiven <48439988+Fexiven@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:21:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/23] rocket: rk3576: place row windows in the CBUF like the
 vendor compiler

The RK3576 splitter counted CBUF entries in 128-byte units while the
registers count 64-byte entries. That gave off-by-one row windows (67 rows
where rknn-toolkit2 2.3.2 uses 68), cumulative CBUF write offsets for later
windows, and the "reuse previous rows" bit (0x1018 bit 31) on 1x1 windows,
where the vendor restarts at entry 0 with the bit clear.

Implement the rule the vendor compiler emits, derived from 1245 compiled
single-layer models (exact on all of them):

 - the input part of the CBUF is a ring of D x 1024 entries of 64 bytes,
   D = 5 when the task input needs more than 4096 entries, else 4
   (0x1018 low bytes, 0x1040 bank flag);
 - a window is the largest run of output rows whose input span, overlap
   rows included, fits the ring;
 - only rows not already in the CBUF are loaded; they are written at the
   running ring position (0x1040 low), the window reads from the position
   of its first row (0x103c low);
 - a window that keeps nothing from the previous one starts at entry 0
   with 0x1018 bit 31 clear (every 1x1 conv, the first conv);
 - 0x401c / 0x40b8 are written from one plane value;
 - regular convs with ic % 16 != 0 keep the real ic - 1 in 0x1028/0x107c.

The first-conv encoder is parameterised on the input size instead of
replaying the 224x224 capture (SSD-MobileNetV2's 300x300 input gets
windows of 134 + 16 rows).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
